# Versioning (caveman)

- The law is `laraplate-stack/.cursor/rules/09-versioning.mdc`. Read it before proposing or cutting a release.
- This repository has no release tool. The only one is `scripts/version.sh` at the stack root: it releases every repository of the stack (application, each `Modules/*` submodule, `laraedge`, UI packages), so it cannot live inside the backend. Releases are cut from the stack, not from this checkout.
- Here: never bump a `version` in any `composer.json`, never write a `CHANGELOG.md` entry, never create a tag by hand, never invent a release command.
- Use conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `feat!:`): level and changelog are read from them.
- The application and each module version themselves. At the end of a plan, task or self-contained feature, once committed and green, ask the user whether to cut a release and motivate the level per affected target. The stack rule says how.
